      "text_raw": "Application of this load to a\ndifferential pair, gives the\nhigh-gain amplifier shown\nin this slide.\nIt is clear that the\ndifferential output signals\nare cancelled out at the\ncommon-Gate point of the\ntransistors M2. The self-\nbiasing is actually a case of\ncommon-mode feedback, as\nexplained in Chapter 8.\nThe gain is moderately\nhigh.\nThere is no biasing prob-\nlem. Current source I\nB\ndetermines all currents.",
